he nation; criticizes McCain for taking the low road.] Obama shown trick-or-treating with daughter Sasha in Chicago.  \n\n(Studio: Brian Williams) Governor Sarah Palin\u2019s failure to release her medical records noted.  \n\n(DeKalb County, Georgia: Michelle Kosinski) The high turnout for early voting featured; scenes shown of lines in Georgia and Arizona, 107-year-old Ada Nettles&#134;&#134; at the polling place in South Carolina; statistics cited. [In line, several VOTERS, National Guardswoman Greer AVERY&#135;\u2013 comment.] [Georgia State University professor Sean RICHEY&#134;- says the campaigns are making appeals to their supporters.] [George Mason University professor Michael McDONALD&#134;- notes the change with most of the early voters being Democrats.] ", "segment_duration": 460, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 922711, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "VYRM3O9SGp", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-31", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 922710, "segment_id": "3ycjvaZoV4", "segment_broadcast_id": "VYRM3O9SGp", "segment_title": "Decision 2008 / Obama Interview (Part II)", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) More of yesterday\u2019s interview with Senator Barack Obama presented. [In Sarasota, Florida, OBAMA \u2013 reacts to concern about one-party control if he wins; comments on a picture of him taking a walk while visiting his sick grandmother in Hawaii and his loss of anonymity; says he hopes the press will show restraint toward his kids.] ", "segment_duration": 230, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63510.0", "legacy_