raeus", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) The ceremony in Tampa to welcome home Gen. David Petraeus, who is taking control of Central Command, shown. ", "segment_duration": 20, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "64190.0", "legacy_segment_id": 922719, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "VYRM3O9SGp", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-31", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 922710, "segment_id": "bKFQfgvCbc", "segment_broadcast_id": "VYRM3O9SGp", "segment_title": "Hot Spots (Baghdad\u2019s Sadr City)", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) Report introduced.  \n\n(Baghdad: Richard Engel) Baghdad's Sadr City visited; scenes shown of fighting last April, the wall that pens in radical Shiite militias, residents playing soccer on one side and followers of Muqtada al-Sadr burning US flags on the other; gun camera video showing militiamen and the bombing of hideouts. [1-6 Infantry PFC Michael URBAN\u2021, Capt. A.J. BOYES - comment on the difference since the wall was built.] [US Ambassador Ryan CROCKER \u2013 says Al Qaeda has been degraded but not defeated.] ", "segment_duration": 150, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "64210.0", "legacy_segment_id": 922720, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "VYRM3O9SGp", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-31", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id"